---
const tabs = [
	{ label: 'Deduplicated and encrypted', icon: ['M12 3 4 7.5v9L12 21l8-4.5v-9Z'] },
	{ label: 'Hosts cannot delete', icon: ['M12 3a9 9 0 1 0 0 18 9 9 0 0 0 0-18Z', 'm5.6 5.6 12.8 12.8'] },
	{
		label: 'Policies as code',
		icon: ['M14 3H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9Z', 'M14 3v6h6M10 13l-2 2 2 2M14 13l2 2-2 2'],
	},
	{ label: 'Find any file', icon: ['M11 4a7 7 0 1 0 0 14 7 7 0 0 0 0-14Z', 'm20 20-3.5-3.5'] },
	{ label: 'Alerts', icon: ['M6 8a6 6 0 0 1 12 0c0 7 3 9 3 9H3s3-2 3-9', 'M10.3 21a1.9 1.9 0 0 0 3.4 0'] },
];
const arrow = 'M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6';
const yaml = `<span class="k">apiVersion:</span> lodestore.io/v1alpha1
<span class="k">kind:</span> BackupPolicy
<span class="k">metadata:</span>
  <span class="k">name:</span> <span class="v">etc-and-home</span>
<span class="k">spec:</span>
  <span class="k">repository:</span> <span class="v">main</span>
  <span class="k">paths:</span> [<span class="v">/etc</span>, <span class="v">/home</span>]
<span class="hl">  <span class="k">schedule:</span>
    <span class="k">cron:</span> <span class="v">30 2 * * *</span>
    <span class="k">timezone:</span> <span class="v">Europe/Kyiv</span></span>
  <span class="k">retention:</span>
    <span class="k">keepDaily:</span> <span class="v">7</span>`;
const hits = [
	{ host: 'web-eu-01', versions: '14 versions', when: 'today 03:00' },
	{ host: 'web-eu-02', versions: '14 versions', when: 'today 03:02' },
	{ host: 'ci-runner-03', versions: '3 versions', when: 'Oct 28' },
];
const alerts = [
	{ ch: 'TG', title: 'Backup failed on pg-main-01', sub: 'ops-telegram · pre-backup hook exited with 1' },
	{ ch: '#', title: 'files-02 is overdue', sub: '#ops-alerts · no successful backup for 36 h' },
	{ ch: '@', title: 'Resolved: pg-main-01 backed up', sub: 'oncall@example.com · 26 minutes later' },
];
---

<section class="wrap" id="feat">
	<div class="sec-head rise">
		<h2>Everything a fleet needs.<br /><span class="em">Backups never pass through the server.</span></h2>
		<p>Five things Lodestore does for an ops team.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="tabs rise paused" role="tablist" id="tabs" aria-label="Features">
		{
			tabs.map((t, i) => (
				<button
					class="tab"
					type="button"
					role="tab"
					id={`tab-${i}`}
					aria-controls={`panel-${i}`}
					aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
					tabindex={i === 0 ? 0 : -1}
					data-t={i}
				>
					<span class="ti">
						<svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
							{t.icon.map((d) => (
								<path d={d} />
							))}
						</svg>
					</span>
					{t.label}
					<i class="prog" />
				</button>
			))
		}
	</div>
	<div class="tabcard rise">
		<div class="pane on" role="tabpanel" id="panel-0" aria-labelledby="tab-0" data-p="0">
			<div>
				<h3>Every chunk stored once, <span class="em">sealed on the host.</span></h3>
				<p>
					Files are cut into content-defined chunks. A chunk that already exists in the repository is not uploaded again,
					across snapshots and across hosts.
				</p>
				<p>
					What leaves the host is compressed, then encrypted with XChaCha20-Poly1305. File names are not readable in the
					bucket either.
				</p>
				<a class="more" href="/docs/adr/0003-object-layout/"
					>How the format works <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d={arrow}></path></svg></a
				>
			</div>
			<div class="viz" id="v0">
				<div class="dd-row">
					<span class="who">web-eu-01 Mon</span><span class="hx">A</span><span class="hx">B</span><span class="hx">C</span
					><span class="hx">D</span>
				</div>
				<div class="dd-row">
					<span class="who">web-eu-01 Tue</span><span class="hx dup" data-d>A</span><span class="hx dup" data-d>B</span
					><span class="hx dup" data-d>C</span><span class="hx lime">E</span>
				</div>
				<div class="dd-row">
					<span class="who">web-eu-02 Tue</span><span class="hx dup" data-d>A</span><span class="hx dup" data-d>B</span
					><span class="hx lime">F</span>
				</div>
				<div class="dd-arrow">
					<svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M6 13l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>stored in your bucket, encrypted
				</div>
				<div class="dd-store">
					{['A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F'].map((c) => <span class="hx st in">{c}</span>)}
				</div>
				<p class="dd-note">11 chunks in three snapshots, 6 stored.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="pane" role="tabpanel" id="panel-1" aria-labelledby="tab-1" data-p="1">
			<div>
				<h3>A taken-over host <span class="em">cannot erase its history.</span></h3>
				<p>
					On S3-compatible storage the key the agents write with has no delete permission. Deletion and cleanup run only on
					the server, in two phases with a wait longer than the longest backup.
				</p>
				<p>It works with S3 Object Lock, so even the server cannot remove data before its time.</p>
				<a class="more" href="/docs/security/threat-model/#agent-credentials"
					>Threat model <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d={arrow}></path></svg></a
				>
			</div>
			<div class="viz log" id="v1">
				<div class="in"><span class="who">agent</span>PUT    data/3f/3f9a…c2e   <span class="good">200 OK</span></div>
				<div class="in"><span class="who">agent</span>PUT    data/8b/8be0…d71   <span class="good">200 OK</span></div>
				<div class="in"><span class="who">attacker</span>DELETE data/3f/3f9a…c2e   <span class="bad">403 AccessDenied</span></div>
				<div class="in"><span class="who">attacker</span>GET    data/3f/3f9a…c2e   <span class="bad">403 AccessDenied</span></div>
				<div class="in"><span class="who">server</span>gc mark   412 unreferenced packs</div>
				<div class="in"><span class="who">server</span>gc wait   longer than the longest backup</div>
				<div class="in"><span class="who">server</span>gc check  still unreferenced: 412</div>
				<div class="in"><span class="who">server</span>gc delete <span class="good">done</span>, dry run available</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="pane" role="tabpanel" id="panel-2" aria-labelledby="tab-2" data-p="2">
			<div>
				<h3>Click it together, <span class="em">or keep it in Git.</span></h3>
				<p>
					Schedules in a time zone with jitter and catch-up of missed runs, retention, upload limits. Edit a policy in the
					interface, or apply the same YAML from your GitOps repository.
				</p>
				<a class="more" href="/docs/guides/policies/"
					>Policies guide <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d={arrow}></path></svg></a
				>
			</div>
			<div class="viz yaml" id="v2">
				<div class="pol">
					<div class="pol-form">
						<div class="fld"><span class="lbl">Name</span><div class="in">etc-and-home</div></div>
						<div class="fld"><span class="lbl">Paths</span><div class="in mono">/etc, /home</div></div>
						<div class="fld"><span class="lbl">Schedule</span><div class="in hl mono">30 2 * * *  ·  Europe/Kyiv</div></div>
						<div class="fld"><span class="lbl">Keep</span><div class="in">daily 7</div></div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="pol-yaml" set:html={yaml} />
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="pane" role="tabpanel" id="panel-3" aria-labelledby="tab-3" data-p="3">
			<div>
				<h3>One search <span class="em">across every host.</span></h3>
				<p>
					Someone deleted a config last week, on a host you don't remember. Search a path or a pattern across the snapshots
					of the whole fleet, pick the version and restore it to that host or another one.
				</p>
				<a class="more" href="/docs/reference/cli/#find-a-file"
					>Find a file <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d={arrow}></path></svg></a
				>
			</div>
			<div class="viz" id="v3">
				<div class="srch">
					<svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle><path d="m20 20-3.5-3.5"></path></svg
					><span id="q">nginx.conf</span><span class="caret"></span>
				</div>
				<div class="res">
					{
						hits.map((h) => (
							<div class="in">
								<span>
									<b>{h.host}</b> <span class="mono">/etc/nginx/nginx.conf</span>
								</span>
								<span class="mono">{h.versions}</span>
								<span class="mono">{h.when}</span>
							</div>
						))
					}
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="pane" role="tabpanel" id="panel-4" aria-labelledby="tab-4" data-p="4">
			<div>
				<h3>Hear about a failed backup <span class="em">before you need it.</span></h3>
				<p>
					Alerts for failed, overdue and offline hosts, failed checks and agent updates. Send them to Telegram, Slack, email
					or a webhook, and scrape Prometheus metrics.
				</p>
				<a class="more" href="/docs/guides/alerts/"
					>Alerts guide <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d={arrow}></path></svg></a
				>
			</div>
			<div class="viz ntf" id="v4">
				{
					alerts.map((a) => (
						<div class="in">
							<span class="ch">{a.ch}</span>
							<p>
								<b>{a.title}</b>
								<br />
								<small>{a.sub}</small>
							</p>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<script>
	import '../../scripts/feature-tabs';
</script>
